4. Spring configuration

Since your application is using the older Spring XML configuration rather than modern application.properties, you can configure it in your existing Spring XML.

For example:

<bean id="aesKeyProvider"
      class="com.new.example.security.AesKeyProvider">
    <constructor-arg
        value="/secure/cmp/aes.key" />
</bean>
<bean id="encryptionService"
      class="com.new.example.security.Aes256GcmEncryptionService">
    <constructor-arg ref="aesKeyProvider" />
</bean>
<bean id="messageSource"
      class="com.new.example.security.SecureMessageSource">
    <property name="basenames">
        <list>
            <value>routine</value>
        </list>
    </property>
    <property name="defaultEncoding"
              value="UTF-8" />
    <property name="encryptionService"
              ref="encryptionService" />
</bean>

If your current application has something like:

<bean id="messageSource"
      class="org.springframework.context.support.ResourceBundleMessageSource">

you replace that class with:

class="com.new.example.security.SecureMessageSource"

The rest can remain substantially the same.

